module extdeps.pin

data pin_authority_note: String = "P1 of the hermetic tool-provisioning lane (docs/plans/hermetic-tool-provisioning-design.md). A mechanical tool dependency is a ToolPin — an exact version identity plus the expected content identity of the binary — never a location and never a range. Both fields are REQUIRED, so a digest-less or range-only pin is unwritable rather than validated (DESIGN section 5 construction, not a post-check). The reconcile compares that ToolPin against the observed row named by its tool. The key lives on the pin side, not as an extra identity on the observed row."

data pin_observed_grain_prerequisite_note: String = "review 44388, corrected: the expected and observed sides were not at the same grain, and this note marks the point they meet. expected_identity above is PER SUBJECT. The observed side now carries that grain explicitly: ResolvedBuildContext stores observed_tool_identities rows, each row names its tool, and toolchain_identity is the derived fold over those rows rather than the authority. A lookup must REFUSE when the named row is missing, and REFUSE when the name is duplicated; silently taking the first row is the absorbing fallback this prerequisite exists to remove. The remaining reconcile work is to compare against the named row for the subject, not against the aggregate. dissolve-on: feature:per-tool-observed-identity-surfaced."
